Teach DOOM-fire-zig to run unattended and report its own frame rate.

This file, alone in the repository, is not Apache-2.0: a patch carries
the upstream lines it modifies, so it is a derivative of DOOM-fire-zig
and inherits that project's license. Nothing here reaches a felis
binary — nix applies it to the upstream source at build time and the
result is a separate program the bench shell runs — so the exception
stops at this file. See the note under "License" in README.md.

Applied by `devshell.nix` to the pinned upstream checkout (GPL-3.0-or-later,
github.com/const-void/DOOM-fire-zig). Upstream is a demo: it blocks on
a keystroke before the fire starts, runs until Ctrl-C, and paints the
frame rate on screen, where the only reader is a human. The cross-
terminal suite needs a fixed-length run whose result it can parse, so
`DOOM_BENCH_SECS` adds one — and nothing else. The fire itself, the
frame it emits and the rate it computes are untouched, which is what
keeps the number comparable with the one upstream shows a human.

The report goes to stderr because stdout *is* the workload: a line
printed there would be more bytes for the terminal under test to draw.

